# Line endings are pinned here because they drifted once already: this repo is
# developed on Windows, and training/train_router.py and calibrate_safety.py --
# shipped by the baseline as LF -- came back as CRLF, which turned a 138-line
# change into a 568-line diff for anyone reviewing it.
#
# Everything is LF, with one deliberate exception: src/ossp_router/heuristic.py
# arrived from the baseline as CRLF and is internally consistent, so it stays
# that way. Converting it would add ~3700 lines of whitespace-only churn to the
# one file a reviewer most needs to read.
#
# It is marked -text rather than "text eol=crlf" on purpose. The latter asks git
# to store an LF blob and hand out CRLF, which would mean renormalizing the
# committed blob -- the very churn we are avoiding -- and until that happened
# the file showed as permanently modified. -text tells git to leave the bytes
# alone in both directions, so the tree stays clean.
* text=auto eol=lf
src/ossp_router/heuristic.py -text
*.npz binary
*.png binary
